@jenncab_ I completely get that 🤍 My family is overseas too, so video calls are part of our reality.

And I truly see the relationship forming - she recognises them in photos, smiles when we say their names, and there’s real interaction during calls. That means so much.

I hold the phone myself (toddlers get curious, so it helps to keep the device in your hands).

@awasha_chan would you like to eat your lunch under a claustrophobic tent that’s resting on your body in hot weather? No? Well then don’t push that on a tiny baby.

My girl hates being covered in a blanket even at night. She’d scream blue murder if it was done to her during the day in our hot Australian weather.

Modesty of breasts, the only body part that actually sustains life, doesn’t matter as much as a happy and fed child.

@chipcherio Yes ,you can absolutely go back and ask about it. PTO and paid sick leave are NOT always the same thing, especially in New York. Some employers keep them separate, and if that’s the case, you may have been entitled to use protected sick leave instead of your PTO.
I would ask, does our company have a separate NY paid sick leave policy, and how is it tracked?
Also moving forward, make sure you’re documenting when you’re sick and how your time is being coded. That part matters more than people think.

