@greatnessdefined That’s exactly why employees should ask questions before accepting major changes tied to accommodations. 
If a company says they “can’t accommodate” something, employees should absolutely ask, Why? What specifically cannot be accommodated? Is there an alternative?Can this be explained in writing?
Documentation and clarification matter A LOT in these situations.

@mgetherz From my understanding potentially yes, but it depends on how your position is classified and whether the accommodation changes the essential structure of the role.
A schedule accommodation request alone does NOT automatically mean someone should lose their salary status.
This is definitely something I would ask HR to explain in writing before agreeing to anything.
